      "sourceTextSha256": "11c6cdd75f53fc48852f2711e1196ee5225f8f43b5f263630fc2f506e7090bfe",
      "text": "Breakfast. Morning excursion to Tierra del Fuego National Park, with lunch and drinks in a large dining tent in the panoramic Cormorant Archipelago area. After a 25- to 40-minute drive, reach Ensenada Zaratiegui, home of the post office at the end of the world, for a short circular walk along the beach and through the forest, with views of Isla Redonda and the Chilean coast across the Beagle Channel. Continue to Lapataia Bay, where National Route 3 ends, the Lapataia and Ovando rivers, Laguna Verde and Lake Acigami (formerly Lake Roca).\n\nAfternoon · Sailing on the Beagle Channel from the tourist pier, around the Isla de los Pájaros, home to skuas, black-browed albatrosses, steamer ducks, geese and gulls; the Isla de los Lobos, with South American sea lions and fur seals; and the Les Eclaireurs Lighthouse, often mistaken for the “Lighthouse at the End of the World”, with colonies of imperial and rock cormorants. Return to the hotel (transfer not included).",
